	)
	(text "This circuit adds colour output to Superboard 600D or C1P Series II Boards.  It has two colour modes:\n  1. Normal RGB (16 colours on black)\n  2. O.S.I.-like (8 Bright colours on 8 darker coloured background, or inverted)\n\nIt uses Composite SYNC from the U75 header, or Separate H/V from the 600D board.\n\nThe output can be configured for:\n  1. RGBI Digital (usually separate sync)\n  2. RGB Analog (usually composite sync)\n\nWhen COLOR_EN is 0 it is in MONO MODE and the DIP SWITCHES determine which\ncolour appears (ie: G=Green, RGBI=white, GR=Amber) for the ON pixels."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.97 196.85 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1938 1.1938)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "da703716-6770-43ac-a5af-420ddf8583a0")
	)
